824
00:06:08,060 --> 00:06:09,520
I see.

825
00:06:14,150 --> 00:06:15,730
Are you leaving this sheet music here?

826
00:06:16,590 --> 00:06:18,190
I'm not going to use it anymore.

827
00:06:18,540 --> 00:06:20,230
Is that so?

828
00:06:21,740 --> 00:06:24,990
Does the college you got a recommendation 
for have a strong band club?

829
00:06:25,490 --> 00:06:27,830
I heard they have a band appreciation society.

830
00:06:28,530 --> 00:06:29,410
How about a band club?

831
00:06:29,410 --> 00:06:30,410
They don't have one.

832
00:06:30,410 --> 00:06:32,120
Are you okay with that, Hazuki?

833
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:34,000
Why?

834
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:35,250
"Why"?

835
00:06:35,250 --> 00:06:39,210
When you were in band, you were aiming 
for the national band competition, right?

836
00:06:39,210 --> 00:06:41,380
You placed pretty well, too.

837
00:06:41,920 --> 00:06:44,760
Getting to nationals was impossible in the end, though.

838
00:06:45,300 --> 00:06:48,390
But I originally wondered 
if I should play until the end of high school.

839
00:06:49,180 --> 00:06:55,390
I figured you'd keep it up even in college. 
You took care of the underclassmen, after all.

840
00:06:57,860 --> 00:06:59,400
I like performing.

841
00:06:59,400 --> 00:07:03,800
But my goal for high school was nationals, so...

842
00:07:03,800 --> 00:07:07,030
You can just find a goal for college.

843
00:07:07,190 --> 00:07:11,700
If the members were together, I might've. 
But everyone's going their separate ways.

844
00:07:11,700 --> 00:07:16,080
It's probably different from track, 
where I participate independently, but...

845
00:07:16,080 --> 00:07:16,870
"But"?

846
00:07:17,710 --> 00:07:19,380
It's kind of a waste.

847
00:07:20,710 --> 00:07:22,000
Thanks.

848
00:07:22,880 --> 00:07:25,800
So? What are you gonna do in college?

849
00:07:25,800 --> 00:07:27,390
First, I'll live by myself.

850
00:07:27,390 --> 00:07:29,050
No, that's not what I meant.

851
00:07:30,680 --> 00:07:33,470
Well, I'll hurry up and graduate, then get a job, I guess.

852
00:07:33,470 --> 00:07:35,480
That's your plan?

853
00:07:40,190 --> 00:07:44,740
I'm going to help with the family business someday...

854
00:07:45,900 --> 00:07:48,860
I see, so that's it.

855
00:07:49,910 --> 00:07:53,910
Man, I'm so dumb! Sorry.

856
00:07:53,910 --> 00:07:57,710
It's all right. I felt much better since you told me.

857
00:08:02,130 --> 00:08:04,300
Riding a moped to school isn't allowed, right?

858
00:08:04,880 --> 00:08:10,430
I told Komiya that 
the Broadcasting Club is filming today.

859
00:08:11,470 --> 00:08:13,890
It's raining, so why don't we save it for another day?

860
00:08:18,390 --> 00:08:20,980
We've collected a whole lot of railroad photos.

861
00:08:20,980 --> 00:08:22,730
Yeah, that's true.

862
00:08:23,270 --> 00:08:25,280
Oh, the one from two days ago.

863
00:08:25,280 --> 00:08:27,070
It's a nice shot, huh?

864
00:08:27,070 --> 00:08:30,490
No way. Well, here's mine.

865
00:08:30,490 --> 00:08:33,530
Well, I've got this, too.

866
00:08:33,950 --> 00:08:35,540
But you've still got a ways to go.

867
00:08:39,580 --> 00:08:43,460
Sorry I'm late. I got you guys a soda to make up for it.

868
00:08:43,460 --> 00:08:47,130
You cleaned up for me! Everything's nice and tidy!

869
00:08:47,630 --> 00:08:50,050
I wanna ride a special limited 
express train for winter break.

870
00:08:50,050 --> 00:08:52,010
The Odakyu Romancecar is a must!

871
00:08:52,010 --> 00:08:53,760
I'll clean this side.

872
00:08:54,510 --> 00:08:56,270
Phew...

873
00:08:56,270 --> 00:08:58,020
Oh, yeah! How's this shot?

874
00:08:58,430 --> 00:09:01,020
Isn't this photo from the other day awesome?

875
00:09:02,900 --> 00:09:04,320
Yeah, it's nice.

876
00:09:04,320 --> 00:09:06,730
But it's a little underexposed, isn't it?

877
00:09:06,730 --> 00:09:09,780
Oh, that's 'cause it was evening.

878
00:09:10,280 --> 00:09:12,570
It's got a nice feel to it, just as it is.

879
00:09:12,570 --> 00:09:17,160
You're going for the prize at a competition, right? The judges are gonna nitpick that sort of thing.

880
00:09:17,160 --> 00:09:18,700
That's probably true.

881
00:09:18,700 --> 00:09:21,670
They're not gonna think, "It's good vice versa," anyway.

882
00:09:21,670 --> 00:09:24,790
If you two get some nice shots, 
enter a competition, 'kay?

883
00:09:27,510 --> 00:09:28,300
By the way...

884
00:09:28,920 --> 00:09:30,220
Who is this?

885
00:09:30,220 --> 00:09:31,300
That's, well...

886
00:09:32,050 --> 00:09:33,800
I'm looking into it at the moment!

887
00:09:42,810 --> 00:09:44,860
This place brings back memories.

888
00:09:44,860 --> 00:09:46,820
We used to play catch here often, huh?

889
00:09:46,820 --> 00:09:50,490
Going out to collect the balls 
from your great wild pitch was a pain.

890
00:09:50,490 --> 00:09:54,200
Shut up. I don't wanna hear 
that from a guy who throws me breaking balls.

891
00:09:54,200 --> 00:09:56,620
You always threw pitches like that back then.

892
00:09:57,330 --> 00:10:01,040
If you knew where the ball was going, 
there'd be no point in throwing a breaking ball.

893
00:10:01,870 --> 00:10:04,330
Your justification for it hasn't changed, either.

894
00:10:07,710 --> 00:10:10,010
Why did things turn out this way?

895
00:10:10,010 --> 00:10:10,840
Huh?

896
00:10:10,840 --> 00:10:14,840
I thought coming back here would be no big deal.

897
00:10:15,300 --> 00:10:17,050
What's that supposed to mean?

898
00:10:17,050 --> 00:10:21,680
Like, I only have the third semester of school to go, 
and I'm just gonna graduate, first of all.

899
00:10:22,810 --> 00:10:24,850
Then, go on to college, I guess.

900
00:10:26,150 --> 00:10:27,760
College, huh?

901
00:10:27,760 --> 00:10:30,070
I happened to run into you.

902
00:10:30,070 --> 00:10:31,610
And you ran into Natsume, too.

903
00:10:32,990 --> 00:10:36,240
What about you, Haruto? 
What are you gonna do after you get a job?

904
00:10:37,530 --> 00:10:38,370
Huh?

905
00:10:38,370 --> 00:10:40,290
I'm gonna work.

906
00:10:40,290 --> 00:10:41,750
What are you gonna make?

907
00:10:41,750 --> 00:10:43,790
An artificial satellite or something.

908
00:10:43,790 --> 00:10:45,880
That's pretty awesome.

909
00:10:45,880 --> 00:10:48,130
Well, I can't make one, though.

910
00:10:49,090 --> 00:10:51,760
How 'bout you, Eita? What are you gonna do 
after you go to college?

911
00:10:51,760 --> 00:10:52,670
Dunno.

912
00:10:53,550 --> 00:10:55,340
Not serious about it, huh?

913
00:10:55,340 --> 00:10:59,050
I just wanted to get entrance exams over 
with early with a general recommendation.

914
00:10:59,050 --> 00:11:02,100
I don't really get it, but did you study hard?

915
00:11:02,770 --> 00:11:06,730
Well, I didn't participate in any clubs, 
and I didn't work part-time over there.

916
00:11:07,350 --> 00:11:10,480
And I'd be looked down 
on if I couldn't at least study well.

917
00:11:10,480 --> 00:11:12,480
What kinda reason is that?

918
00:11:13,240 --> 00:11:16,950
Oh, by the way, if you're free, 
you can just ask Morikawa-san to hang out.

919
00:11:16,950 --> 00:11:18,910
I would've asked if I could.

920
00:11:18,910 --> 00:11:23,690
I'll seem like I'm asking for too much 
if I do things immediately after adding her on LINE.

921
00:11:24,250 --> 00:11:27,630
Don't come crying to me if it gets hard to say anything to her after not contacting her for days.

922
00:11:27,630 --> 00:11:30,130
That's happened before.

923
00:11:34,170 --> 00:11:34,210
Mio Natsume

